/-
# PF.SecantSizeLower_r197

★★★ 2026-08-05 — THE SECANT SIZE LOWER BOUND, FOR EVERY CURVE ★★★

The CL half of the universal secant window (r193 was the CU half): the
addition triple cannot be uniformly small —

  **`Δ⁴ · H₁²H₂² ≤ CLsec · max(|DDz|, |Sfz|, |Prz|)`**

with `CLsec` an explicit polynomial in `|b₂|,|b₄|,|b₆|,|b₈|` alone.

Route (all certificate-level, no divisions until the final cancellation):
1. Size-bound the eight r195/r196 Bézout cofactors termwise:
   `|cert| ≤ S·H₁⁶H₂` with `S` the coefficient-absolute-sum (this file is
   generated by `codex/gen_r197.py`; every bound is `linarith` over
   `term_bound` facts).
2. Corner lemmas: through the certificates,
   `H₂³·Psi(a₁,b₁)² ≤ S_Ψ·H₁⁶H₂·max(|DDz|,|Sfz|)` and likewise for `Phi`
   with `Prz` — whichever of `|a₂|, |b₂|` realizes `H₂`, one of the twin
   certificates covers it.
3. Square r175's lower bound `Δ²H₁⁴ ≤ CL·max|Φ||Ψ|` and chain:
   `Δ⁴H₁⁸H₂³ ≤ CL²·H₂³·max(Φ²,Ψ²) ≤ CL²·S·H₁⁶H₂·M`; cancel `H₁⁶H₂`.

Constants at 5077a1 (sanity, from the generator): S-sums 386/97/1665/196
and 6613/245/26681/488 — the uniform price, as with r175's κ.

Together with r193 (upper), r196 (content ∣ Δ⁶), and r148e (quadratic-root
heights, already generic), this completes the estimate layer of the
universal quasi-parallelogram window; the window assembly and the limit
into r171's generic canonical height are the remaining (bookkeeping)
stones of the coefficient-only rank pipeline.

Kernel axioms ⊆ `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`; no `sorry`,
no project axioms, no `native_decide`.

Author: Pablo Cohen + Claude. 2026-08-05.
-/
